|WKBSYNTAX
======

|CKBsmartequip|WKB
|CKBsmartequip -v|WKB

DESCRIPTION
===========

|YKOUses the same equipment-power scores as |CKBgearcheck|YKO to improve your
currently equipped armour and weapons. Smart equip fills open equipment slots
and replaces equipped items only when the new combination has a higher,
high-confidence score.

Hand equipment is evaluated as a complete setup rather than one item at a
time. Smart equip compares a two-handed weapon against compatible dual-wielded
weapon pairs and weapon-and-shield combinations. A secondary weapon's offense
is weighted for its reduced attack rate, and your trained weapon
specialization adds its normal combat advantage or disadvantage to the score.

Only armour and weapons carried directly in your inventory are considered.
Equipment stored inside bags or other containers is left where it is.
Installed implants and other internal equipment are never changed.

Smart equip applies the best compatible hand setup atomically, then checks
other armour improvements one at a time. If an item cannot be worn or wielded
because of a character requirement, curse, size restriction, weapon
combination, or another equipment rule, your displaced equipment is restored
and that setup or item is skipped.

You cannot use smart equip during combat, while dead, or while phased out.
Use |CKBgearcheck|YKO afterward when you want to inspect the detailed score
behind each decision. Use |CKBloadout|YKO to save the resulting equipment as a
named preset.

VERBOSE MODE
============

|CKBsmartequip -v|YKO performs the same equipment changes and then shows every
standard equipment slot. For each slot it lists the currently equipped item,
all inventory candidates that can use that slot, the candidate and displaced
item scores, score difference, gearcheck classification, confidence, items
that would be replaced, rejection reason, and final decision.

Each slot begins with a bright |GKBSELECTED|YKO summary. Winning equipment is
shown first with a |GKB★ WINNER|YKO badge, while kept current gear, rejected
items, replaced gear, and unselected candidates use distinct labels and
colors.

Equipment inside containers and implants also appear with an explanation of
why smart equip did not consider them.
